    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0126" n="94" xml:id="pg94"/>

                <head>44. Memorandum From the Chairman of the Task Force on Latin America (Berle) to Secretary of State
                        Rusk<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d44-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-02-14">February 14,
                        1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Cuba</item>
                </list>
                <p>As the White House conference<anchor n="1" xml:id="d44-f2"/> broke up, we <list>
                        <label>(a)</label>
                        <item>arranged leadership for the camps;</item>
                        <label>(b)</label>
                        <item>kept the operation standing;</item>
                        <label>(c)</label>
                        <item>agreed the situation would need review not later than early next
                            week.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Should we not set up another White House meeting late this
                    week to determine the next step?</p>
                <p>In this connection the CIA paper<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d44-f3"/> I referred to in an earlier memorandum<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d44-f4"/> has probably reached you. I have seen it. It suggests that
                    dismantling the Cuban operation may mean explosions in three or four countries
                    in Central America. If this is accurate, we should be prepared for the
                    consequences of dismantling.</p>
                <p>The countries involved are [<hi rendition="#italic">1 line of source text not
                        declassified</hi>] Nicaragua and Guatemala.</p>
                <p>I think the danger may be a little overdrawn [<hi rendition="#italic">1½ lines of
                        source text not declassified</hi>] though Guatemala may be an issue, but we
                    do have to get our lines straight.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
